; liveissues.eval - live validation's boxes (editor-updates P2).
;
; `editor issues` re-runs the live check and prints one "editor box" line per
; square the map would box on the VIEWED level, then the Check badge's count.
;
; PART A - lost items, on eval_arena. Two items go on 3,3 and 4,3, then walls
; seal that pair of squares off from the rest of the room: ONE finding (the
; report counts lost items rather than listing them) but TWO boxes.
;
; PART B - a broken stair pair. tools/EditorTest.py deletes crypt2's stair
; back up to crypt1 before this runs (and restores it after), so crypt1's
; stair down at 1,1 is unpaired: boxed on crypt1 where it stands, AND on
; crypt2 at 1,1 where its partner should be.

logecho on
reset
echo --- A: baseline ---
editor issues
echo --- A: two items walled in ---
editor place items crypt_token 3 3
editor place items crypt_token 4 3
editor fill walls wall_marble rect 2 2 5 2
editor fill walls wall_marble rect 2 4 5 4
editor fill walls wall_marble rect 2 3 2 3
editor fill walls wall_marble rect 5 3 5 3
editor issues
echo --- B: the stair's own end ---
goto crypt1
editor issues
echo --- B: the far end ---
goto crypt2
editor issues
